Research decision memo — Stage 4
Title: Statistical Equilibrium and Maximum Entropy
Status: NOT STARTED

Central hypothesis: Under what constraints, invariant measures and equilibrium policies does the heterogeneous-agent distribution admit a rigorous entropy-based characterization?

Feasibility prior:
Conditional: household optimality and competitive clearing alone do not imply Boltzmann-Gibbs or maximum entropy; require derivable invariant or optimization conditions.

Core economic distinction:
Direct invariant distribution of verified GE policy functions, with and without reversible dynamics

Conditions to check:
1. Stationary distribution operator or master equation
2. Resource/moment constraints and probability normalization
3. Conditional entropy optimization and Lagrange multipliers
4. Detailed balance or stationary probability-current identities

Pass / fail criterion:
Prove a conditional characterization or report an informative failure; do not impose entropy as an equilibrium axiom.

The project reports negative feasibility results when a kinetic, entropy, adaptive-trading, or heuristic-firm mechanism cannot be reconciled with optimization and equilibrium. Do not silently weaken rational expectations or drop clearing equations.

Evidence status: no derived theorems, numerical solutions or validated simulations committed yet.
